### Field-by-Field Explanation

| Field | Data Element / Type | Reasoning |
|---|---|---|
| `CLIENT` | `MANDT` | Mandatory first key field for every client-dependent table in SAP. |
| `REQUEST_UUID` | `SYSUUID_X16` (RAW16) | **Technical primary key.** See "UUID" explanation below. |
| `REQUEST_NO` | `CHAR10` | **Semantic/business key.** Human-readable request number (e.g. `SDR0000001`), generated in a Determination (Step 8) — never used as the DB key. |
| `CUSTOMER` | `KUNNR` | Standard customer number data element — enables automatic value help & matches `I_Customer` association in Step 4. |
| `MATERIAL` | `MATNR` | Standard material number data element (CHAR18, conversion exit `MATN1`) — matches `I_Product`. |
| `PLANT` | `WERKS_D` | Standard plant data element — matches `I_Plant`. |
| `QUANTITY` | `abap.quan(13,3)` | Built-in quantity type, 3 decimals — same precision as standard `MENGE`-based fields. No DDIC-level unit reference is set here (see "Currency/Quantity Reference" below — that's done at CDS level). |
| `UOM` | `MEINS` | Standard unit-of-measure data element (CHAR3, conversion exit `CUNIT`). |
| `REQ_DATE` | `DATS` | Date the sample request was raised. |
| `REQ_STATUS` | `CHAR1` | Status code. Values used across this project: `N` = New, `V` = Validated, `A` = Approved, `R` = Rejected. This drives the `GET_STATUS_TEXT` utility method (Step 3) and the Criticality annotation (Step 4). |
| `REJECT_REASON` | `CHAR100` | Free-text reason, populated only when status = `R`. |
| `APPROVED_BY` | `SYUNAME` | User ID of the approver — set by the Approve action (Step 8), never editable by the end user directly. |
| `APPROVED_ON` | `DATS` | Date of approval — set by the Approve action. |
| `CREATED_BY` / `CREATED_AT` | `SYUNAME` / `TIMESTAMPL` | Standard RAP admin fields — auto-populated by the framework at create time when mapped via `@Semantics.systemDateTime.createdAt/createdBy` in Step 4. |
| `LAST_CHANGED_BY` / `LAST_CHANGED_AT` | `SYUNAME` / `TIMESTAMPL` | Global last-change tracking — used for cross-system change propagation (delta pulls, side-effects). |
| `LOCAL_LAST_CHANGED_AT` | `TIMESTAMPL` | **ETag field.** See explanation below — separate from the global field because ETag must reflect only *this system's* local change, not replicated changes from elsewhere. |

