### Explanation
- **`CX_NO_CHECK`** — chosen because RAP validation/action failures are *expected, handled* outcomes, not fatal programming errors; they must not force `TRY/CATCH` everywhere they're raised (unlike `CX_STATIC_CHECK`).
- **`IF_T100_MESSAGE`** — standard interface that ties an exception instance to a T100 message class entry (`msgid`/`msgno`) plus up to 4 dynamic attributes (`attr1`–`attr4`) that map instance attributes (like `material`, `customer`) into the message placeholders `&1`, `&2` at display time.
- **`IF_ABAP_BEHV_MESSAGE`** — a marker interface (no methods) required for the object to be assignable to `reported-<entity>-%msg` in RAP handler methods.
- **`attr1`-style constants** — each `BEGIN OF ... END OF` structure names *which instance attribute* fills which placeholder, so `WITH material customer` style manual concatenation is never needed — Rule 15 satisfied.

