```abap
CLASS zcl_sdt_sample_util DEFINITION
  PUBLIC
  FINAL
  CREATE PUBLIC .

  PUBLIC SECTION.

    CONSTANTS mc_status_new       TYPE c LENGTH 1 VALUE 'N'.
    CONSTANTS mc_status_validated TYPE c LENGTH 1 VALUE 'V'.
    CONSTANTS mc_status_approved  TYPE c LENGTH 1 VALUE 'A'.
    CONSTANTS mc_status_rejected  TYPE c LENGTH 1 VALUE 'R'.

    CONSTANTS mc_req_prefix     TYPE c LENGTH 3 VALUE 'SDR'.
    CONSTANTS mc_req_no_digits  TYPE i VALUE 7.

    CONSTANTS mc_max_sample_qty TYPE p LENGTH 8 DECIMALS 3 VALUE '50.000'.
    CONSTANTS mc_monthly_cap    TYPE i VALUE 5.

    CLASS-METHODS get_max_sample_qty
      RETURNING VALUE(rv_max_qty) TYPE p LENGTH 8 DECIMALS 3.

    CLASS-METHODS get_status_text
      IMPORTING iv_status      TYPE c
      RETURNING VALUE(rv_text) TYPE string.

    CLASS-METHODS is_monthly_cap_hit
      IMPORTING iv_customer   TYPE kunnr
      RETURNING VALUE(rv_hit) TYPE abap_bool.

ENDCLASS.


CLASS zcl_sdt_sample_util IMPLEMENTATION.

  METHOD get_max_sample_qty.
    rv_max_qty = mc_max_sample_qty.
  ENDMETHOD.


  METHOD get_status_text.
    CASE iv_status.
      WHEN mc_status_new.
        rv_text = 'New'.
      WHEN mc_status_validated.
        rv_text = 'Validated'.
      WHEN mc_status_approved.
        rv_text = 'Approved'.
      WHEN mc_status_rejected.
        rv_text = 'Rejected'.
      WHEN OTHERS.
        rv_text = 'Unknown'.
    ENDCASE.
  ENDMETHOD.


  METHOD is_monthly_cap_hit.
    DATA lv_count       TYPE i.
    DATA lv_today       TYPE dats.
    DATA lv_month_start TYPE dats.

    lv_today = cl_abap_context_info=>get_system_date( ).
    lv_month_start = lv_today.
    lv_month_start+6(2) = '01'.

    SELECT COUNT(*)
      FROM zsdt_sample_req
      WHERE customer   = @iv_customer
        AND req_status <> @mc_status_rejected
        AND req_date   >= @lv_month_start
        AND req_date   <= @lv_today
      INTO @lv_count.

    rv_hit = xsdbool( lv_count >= mc_monthly_cap ).
  ENDMETHOD.

ENDCLASS.
```

### Method Explanations
- **`GET_MAX_SAMPLE_QTY`** — returns the business-configured ceiling per sample request (50 units). Kept as a method (not a public constant reference directly) so that in a future phase this could read from a Customizing table without changing any caller's code — this is what "reusable" means in practice.
- **`GET_STATUS_TEXT`** — single source of truth for status display text, used identically by the ALV report and available for any future CDS text-association replacement.
- **`IS_MONTHLY_CAP_HIT`** — counts non-rejected requests for the customer from the 1st of the current month through today; returns `abap_true` if the count has already reached the cap (5). Uses `xsdbool()` instead of a manual `IF...THEN...ELSE` — Clean ABAP style.

