### Concept Explanations
- **`strict ( 2 )`** — the strictest RAP compliance level; catches issues like using `%control` incorrectly, non-exclusive lock declarations, or calling non-RAP-approved statements inside handler methods, *at design time* instead of at runtime.
- **`lock master`** — this entity owns its own optimistic/pessimistic lock (via the standard RAP lock enqueue mechanism); since there's no parent/child composition here, the root is trivially also the lock master.
- **`authorization master ( instance )`** — every instance-level operation (Create/Update/Delete/Action) triggers an authorization check via `AUTHORITY-CHECK` inside a dedicated check method you'd implement in `get_instance_authorizations` (optional; if omitted, RAP defaults to allow — for the assessment I've kept this declarative-only and noted below that a production build would add an explicit instance-authorization method using a custom object like `ZSDT_APPR`, created via SU21, checked against `ACTVT` values 01/02/06 and custom activities for Approve/Reject).
- **`etag master LocalLastChangedAt`** — every Update/Action request must supply the ETag it last read; a mismatch → HTTP 412, protecting against two approvers processing stale data.
- **`field ( readonly )`** — these fields can never be set by an OData PATCH from the UI; they're only ever set by RAP itself (admin fields) or by our own determinations/actions (RequestNo, ReqStatus, ApprovedBy/On, RejectReason).
- **`field ( mandatory )`** — Fiori Elements will block Save until these are filled; this is UI-level enforcement, distinct from (and in addition to) the save-time *content* validations in Step 8.
- **`action ... result [1] $self`** — each action returns exactly one instance of the same entity (`$self`), which lets the UI immediately refresh the row's new status without a separate GET round-trip.
- **`determination ... on modify { create; }`** — triggers automatically and synchronously right after a Create is registered (before Save), used here to stamp default values.
- **`determination ... on modify { field Material; }`** — triggers whenever `Material` changes (on Create or Update), used to auto-derive `Uom`.
- **`validation ... on save { create; field Material; }`** — triggers at Save time, for new instances, when `Material` was touched — keeps validation cost minimal (doesn't re-validate untouched fields).
- **`mapping for zsdt_sample_req`** — explicit CDS-alias-to-DB-column mapping; required because our CDS field names (`RequestUUID`) differ in casing/style from the DB column names (`request_uuid`).
- **Projection BDEF `use` statements** — nothing here has its own logic; it purely re-exposes the root's capabilities to the projection layer that the Service Definition will publish.

### Testing Steps
1. Activate the abstract entity first, then the root BDEF, then the projection BDEF.
2. Check the **Problems** view in ADT — should show zero errors/warnings for `strict(2)` compliance.
3. Use **ADT → Behavior Definition → "Generate Behavior Implementation"** quick-fix — this auto-creates the `ZBP_I_SAMPLEREQUEST` class skeleton with correctly-typed method signatures (do this before Step 8 so you paste logic into the generated stubs rather than typing signatures by hand).

