## STEP 9 — Service Definition

### Why we create it
Declares *which* CDS projection(s) are exposed as an OData service — the bridge between your RAP BO and the outside world (Fiori, Postman, any OData consumer).

### Where it is used
Consumed exclusively by the Service Binding (Step 10).

### How RAP uses it
Purely declarative — no runtime logic. One Service Definition can expose multiple projections (e.g., if you later add a "Sample Request Approval Worklist" projection), all published together under one OData service via a single Service Binding.

### Common mistakes
- Exposing the **root** view (`ZI_SampleRequest`) instead of the **projection** (`ZC_SampleRequest`) — root views are for reuse by other CDS/BDEFs, not direct UI exposure.
- Choosing an entity set name that clashes with another already-published service in your system.

### Activation order
After Step 6 (Metadata Extension) and Step 7 (both BDEFs) are active — though technically only the projection view (Step 5) is a hard dependency, best practice is to only build the Service Definition once the full BO (including behavior) is complete.

---

