### Explanation
- **`expose ... as SampleRequest`** — `SampleRequest` becomes the OData **entity set name** clients see in the service (`/SampleRequest`), independent of the technical CDS view name — lets you rename the underlying view later without breaking API consumers.

### Testing Steps
1. Activate.
2. In ADT, right-click the Service Definition → **Preview** — this does an ad-hoc, unpublished test render (separate from the formal Service Binding preview in Step 11).

### Expected Output
Activates with no errors; ADT's built-in preview (if used) shows a basic list of sample requests.

### Common Errors & Fixes

| Error | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `CDS view ZC_SampleRequest cannot be exposed - not transactional_query` | Forgot `provider contract transactional_query` in Step 5 | Re-check Step 5's projection view header |
| `Entity set name already in use` | Another service definition in the system already uses `SampleRequest` | Rename the alias, e.g. `as SampleRequestSet` |

